ted control (T1), with each treatment applied to five trees constituting the experimental unit. The microbial biostimulants differed in their microbial composition, application rate, and primary mode of action, including nitrogen fixation, phosphorus solubilization, nutrient solubilization, and phytohormone production. The microbial biostimulants were applied by injection into the wetted root zone at a depth of approximately 15 cm during the first week of April 2023, 2024, and 2025 in both fields. For data interpretation throughout the manuscript, treatments were grouped according to their predominant mode of action, as reported by the manufacturers, into nitrogen-fixing (T2, T5, T6, and T9), combined nitrogen-fixing and phosphorus-solubilizing (T3 and T7), phosphorus-solubilizing (T4), nutrient-solubilizing (T8), and the untreated control (T1). To minimize border effects, a one-tree-row buffer was maintained between adjacent treatments within each block and between blocks."]}